{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And after this, Abraham buried Sarah his wife in the cave of the field of Machpelah, etc. — the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan\"</b> is that Scripture returns to mention the field and the place and the land, because the entire passage mentioned the children of Heth and Ephron the Hittite; therefore at the end it mentions that it is in the land of Canaan, which is the land of Israel. And so too it says at the beginning of the passage, \"in Kiryat-Arba — the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan,\" and all this is to explain that the righteous woman died in the land of Israel and was buried there, for the Hittites are among the families of Canaan. In my opinion, the reason of the verses is nothing other than to mention that it is the land of Canaan, not the land of the Philistines, for since it says, \"And Abraham sojourned in the land of the Philistines many days\" (Genesis 21:34), and all his sojournings in that land were in Gerar and the wadi of Gerar and Beersheba, and from there to Hebron and from Hebron to there, therefore it mentions that Hebron is in the land of the Canaanite who dwells in that hill country, not in the land of the Philistines mentioned in connection with Abraham. And at the end it adds to make known the cave, which is in the field of Machpelah facing Mamre, for this is the name known for it. And this passage was written to make known the kindness of HaShem with Abraham, that he was a prince of Elohim in the land to which he came to sojourn, and the individual and all the people would call him \"my lord,\" while he did not say thus to them, for he was a prince and great, and also in his lifetime He fulfilled for him \"and I will make your name great, and be a blessing,\" and his wife died and was buried in the inheritance of HaShem. And furthermore, Scripture wanted to inform us of the burial place of the Patriarchs, since we are obligated to honor the burial place of our holy forefathers. And our Sages said (Bava Batra 16a) that this too was among the trials of Abraham, that he sought a place to bury Sarah and did not find one until he purchased it. And I do not know the reason for the words of Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra], who says: to declare the superiority of the land of Israel for the living and for the dead, and also to fulfill for him the word of HaShem, that it be an inheritance to him — for what superiority does the land have in this, that he did not transport her to another land to bury her? And the word of HaShem to Abraham was concerning the entire land and was fulfilled only in his descendants."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:40.834790250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}